June 8, Round Carrots
Twirl, twirl, twirl!

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.730
Art Room B

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.100
Today, we will be making shapes out of clay.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.540
Did you bring a sprayer, a rag
and some shoes?

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:37.840
I borrowed this from someone in
Group B who already did theirs.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.140
Please make an exact replica, like this.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.940
On a side note, the shoes I'm wearing
today cost 14,700 yen.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.890
I'll confiscate anyone's shoes that
are more expensive than these.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.950
Please come forward.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:55.360
She's a tyrant.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:55.790
Step 1
Bring some shoes!
She's a tyrant.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.310
Step 1
Bring some shoes!

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:00.260
What kind did you bring, Yunocchi?

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.030
I brought the loafers that I usually use.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.030
Tadaa!

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:07.030
I brought the indoor slippers that I
wore in elementary school.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:09.170
I brought my old shoes too.

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:11.800
I thought it would be good to
keep them as a memento.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.820
Yuno, what's your shoe size?

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:25.120
21.5...
(Women's size 6 in the US.)

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.820
I brought my old ones too.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.260
Tadaa!

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:32.160
Wow, skates! Amazing!

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:36.230
My parents bought them for me with
what little money they had.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.200
Oh? So, they're a memento.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.610
They don't stand!

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.400
They don't, do they?

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.740
Oh well...

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.480
I guess I'll get the ones I have
in my shoe compartment.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.610
Hey, I brought two pairs.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:53.710
I'll lend you one.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.080
Thank you very much.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.080
It's nothing.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.050
Sorry, they're filthy though.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.250
GUH

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.100
Hey!

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.100
What are you doing, Miya-chan?!
Hey!

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.560
What are you doing, Miya-chan?!

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:15.700
I always feel like smelling
things that look smelly.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.640
That really hurts...

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:18.040
Step 2
Knead the clay well and shape it.
Paper clay
That really hurts...

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.600
Step 2
Knead the clay well and shape it.
Paper clay

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.510
Knead, knead, knead, knead...

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.480
It feels nice and cold!
Knead, knead, knead, knead...

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.310
I'm feeling hungry.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.780
This is like cooking.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.810
You're right.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:34.190
Homemade bread!

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.920
Udon, soba!

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.550
Pizza!

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.160
Miya-chan, you made it so thin!

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:45.700
All right!

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.700
The overall shape looks good.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.040
I should work on the details.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.660
Oh?

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:57.510
Yunocchi, that's larger than the actual object.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:04:59.310
It's just your imagination!

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.750
No, it's quite a bit bigger.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.380
No, it's not!
No, it's quite a bit bigger.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:09.060
You have to place a damp cloth over
the clay you aren't using.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.490
Okay!

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.490
Make sure you spray the clay
that you are using.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:18.400
If it dries out, it's difficult to get it back the
way it used to be even if you wet it.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.070
It's important to keep it watered.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:26.110
You mustn't be careless and
think you can hold off on it!

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:28.610
Things will turn bad right away!

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:33.310
In spirit, I'm still in my teens.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.940
How much of that was about clay?

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:37.950
Once you've shaped it, let it dry.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:40.190
Step 3
Dry it.
Once you've shaped it, let it dry.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.320
Step 3
Dry it.
We're going to color them afterwards.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.460
Step 3
Dry it.
Okay!

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:43.950
Okay!

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:48.000
I'm getting sleepy.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.000
Yunocchi, you don't have much time left!

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.620
Fight, fight!

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:57.530
Maybe some fairies will make it
for me while I'm sleeping.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.470
Yunnochi?

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:00.110
Step 4
Paint it!
Yunnochi?

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.440
Step 4
Paint it!

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.510
Wow, it's looking pretty good.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.140
Yeah...

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:19.090
What?!

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.090
Huh?!

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.860
Miya-chan, did I paint this?

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:26.320
Or did something show up?!

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.560
Who knows?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.510
All right, time's up!

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:33.970
You can take your work home.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:36.110
Clean off your desks!

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:36.910
Huh?

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:37.910
We don't have to turn in our work?
Huh?

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.750
We don't have to turn in our work?

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:40.750
That's right!

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.820
Take one of these and pass the rest
to the person behind you.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:49.120
Also, I want you to write a paper
about today's class.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:50.120
Huh?

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:54.160
Well, everyone's designs are different.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.630
I'm not sure how I should judge them.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.660
You're an art teacher.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:05.870
Sae...

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.010
Why if it isn't Sae!

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.180
Natsume...

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.150
Are you having a chat with the
combustible garbage?

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:12.770
You idiot!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:20.710
U-Umm, uhh, Principal, good morning.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.590
It's noon.

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:23.690
Shut up!

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:25.130
Are you fighting?

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.030
No, we're not fighting.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.100
This is just one-sided.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:35.100
True friends share a closer bond when
they make peace after a fight.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.370
It happened for me.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.370
A bond?

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.380
Friendship is a beautiful thing.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:45.310
The fact that you can fight is
proof that you are close.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:48.280
Well, be careful on your way home.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.990
H-He says we're friends.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:53.950
We're not?

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:58.130
Oh, I've been keeping Hiro waiting.

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.750
I'm going.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.420
I've got friends waiting for me too!

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.960
Goodbye!

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.570
What's she mad about?

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:12.510
I'm glad to have you over.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:15.410
Your daughter seems very smart.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:17.180
I've never met her though.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.280
You're too kind.

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:21.250
We were worried about whether she
was doing all right by herself.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:26.020
Compared to other girls her age,
she seems very reliable.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.920
I've never met her though.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:28.920
You're too kind.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:33.860
I'm just glad that she isn't
causing you any trouble.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.130
Thank you very much for the meat buns!

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.600
Please give your daughter my regards.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.860
I've never met her though.

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:47.140
Oh, did you two just come back?

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:50.740
Yes, it took a while to dry.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:51.810
Dry?

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:54.150
Hiro, take a look a this!

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.420
Shoes?

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:58.540
Oh, they're made out of clay. Amazing!

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:01.390
We're going to show them to Sae too!

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:03.320
Sae!

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:05.950
Oh, Sae is working right now.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:07.860
Huh?

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.830
Sae fell asleep at her desk again.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.840
I did it again?

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:23.440
I'm going to sleep in bed for a bit.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:25.640
Huh?

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:30.080
Huh?! U-Umm, who is that?

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.090
Shoes beside the bed?

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:33.710
Which means...

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.520
Who are you?!

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:42.360
Miyako, you're the only one who'd
pull a prank like this!

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.770
What is it, Sae?

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.500
It's nothing!

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.470
Sorry for bothering you!

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:55.830
We're coming in!

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:01.100
Why do you think Sae was in such a
panic when she came to my room?

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:03.850
A text message?

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:04.850
Yeah...

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:07.120
Oh, it's from my mom.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:12.890
She says, "Is school finished?
How do you spend days like this?"

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:13.760
Oh?

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:13.890
New Message
Yeah, it's finished.
On days like this,
I usually relax at home.
Oh?

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:15.930
New Message
Yeah, it's finished.
On days like this,
I usually relax at home.
Yeah, it's finished.

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.770
New Message
Yeah, it's finished.
On days like this,
I usually relax at home.
On days like this, I usually relax at home.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:20.730
On days like this, I usually relax at home.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:22.140
Yeah!

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:22.900
Send
Yeah!

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:23.600
Send

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:26.470
I wonder why she's asking me that?

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.940
How mysterious...

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:31.850
That's odd...

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:33.910
She should be relaxing now.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.850
Did something happen after you texted her?

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:39.480
What?!
Yuno! Yuno! Yuno!

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:42.220
Wh-Why are you here?

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:43.620
Oh, Yuno!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.730
I see, you went out.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:49.360
Where were you going with all
those stuffed animals?

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:50.660
When did you come?

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.930
I was downstairs all this time.

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:58.440
Well, I took a day off, and the two of us
went to Yokohama yesterday.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.240
We were planning on going
straight home today,

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:04.370
but you told me that you finished
school at noon.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.880
I wanted to meet the landlord here

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:11.690
and thought that we should pay you a visit.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.620
It would have been nice if you
could have come with us,

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:17.360
but we decided on it on such short notice.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.260
We felt like we were young again.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.730
We even rode on the merry-go-round.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:27.090
Your father rode on the horse
and I rode in the carriage.

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:31.630
I'm glad I didn't go.

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:36.530
Umm...

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:40.470
Miya-chan, I'd like you to meet my parents.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.140
I'm her mother.

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:43.370
I'm her father.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.000
Hello.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.710
And this is Miya-chan.

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:50.140
Please to meet you, I'm Miyako.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.480
Pleased to meet you!

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.610
Yuno's told me so much about you.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:59.020
This is the girl who's good at
drawing and eats a lot.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:01.820
She's the one who doesn't have any
money and is always hungry.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.220
They don't have "X" marks.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:04.320
Meat Buns
They don't have "X" marks.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:05.960
Meat Buns
Oh, this is a souvenir from Yokohama.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:07.090
Oh, this is a souvenir from Yokohama.

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:09.430
We thought it would be best to get something
you could eat right away,

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:11.230
so we got you meat buns.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.990
What wonderful parents!

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:16.060
Thank you for the food!

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:20.270
Delicious!

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:24.400
I'd like my mom and dad to try this!

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:27.510
What a nice girl!

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:30.850
Thank you for the food!

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:33.920
I'm going to call Sae and Hiro.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.550
Okay!

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:41.830
Your hair's grown out a little since
the last time I saw you.

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:44.430
Huh? Y-You think so?

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:48.430
Yeah, you look a little more mature too.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.340
Th-That's not true!

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:55.300
Y-You've got more white hairs, Dad!

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.640
Darling!

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:02.480
Your room is very clean.

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:05.290
It was a little messier at home.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:07.390
What? Really?

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:10.020
The floor and the kitchen are nicely swept.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.130
It's short.

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:15.090
This isn't Yuno's hair color.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:19.630
Yuno, you have a cat with
hair like this, don't you?

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:20.700
Don't you?

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:23.000
Wh-What's wrong, Dad?

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:27.140
Is there a boy you like?

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.480
Why are you asking that?

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:31.440
I don't have anyone.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.650
Come on in!

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:34.810
Pleased to meet you.

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:36.480
I'm coming in!

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.610
I-I'm coming in.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.220
It's you, isn't it?!

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:48.060
Sorry, I had the wrong idea.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.130
I'm really sorry.

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.930
I-It's all right.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:55.840
Hello, we're always hanging out with Yuno.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:14:01.110
